 "article_notes": "Prospective Onderstepoort study (Jan-Feb 2006) of 36 dogs with B. rossi babesiosis recruited into three admission glucose groups of 12 (hypo-, normo-, hyperglycaemic). Survivors only: dogs that died and mildly affected outpatients were excluded, so the comparison is within hospitalised survivors. Samples were taken before treatment. Variables that were not significant in the three-group Kruskal-Wallis test (age, weight, duration of illness, time since last meal, pulse, respiratory rate, ACTH, TSH) are attached to S1 with the three-group P value. Length of hospital stay (P = 0.092) was also compared but is an outcome, not a marker, and was not extracted. Units in the converted text lost the 'L' (e.g. 'nmol/ '); values copied as printed. Diagnosis by capillary smear; B. vogeli and E. canis excluded by PCR-RLB. Cohort may overlap other Onderstepoort endocrine studies by the same first author.",
